        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Under most circumstances, an employee who returns from CFRA will be reinstated to his or her original job or to an equivalent job with equivalent pay, benefits, and other employment terms and conditions. However, an employee has no greater right to reinstatement than if she or he had been continuously employed rather than on leave. In addition, employees who do not return to work generally are not entitled to an accrual of seniority or employment benefits that may have occurred during a leave period.",
